### Permutation check

Of the {{S2:n_de}} genes called differentially expressed, {{S2:n_de_perm_below_005}} also had a
permutation p-value below 0.05. With six samples in two groups of three, the permutation test
cannot reach very small p-values, so it is reported as a check on direction and rough strength
rather than as a second significance call.

## Discussion

SYNX-7 changes the expression of the {{S2:n_de}} genes reported above in SYNTH-CL1, with the
fold changes given in Table 1 and Supplementary Table S1. The modest number of replicates bounds
what can be detected: genes with low expression or small changes will be missed, and the list in
Supplementary Table S1 should be read as the changes this design could detect rather than as a
complete account of the compound's effect.

Two choices in the analysis deserve mention. Quantification with selective alignment and
aggregation with tximport lets reads that are compatible with several isoforms of a gene count
towards that gene without forcing an early assignment to one isoform. The permutation check
reports a model-free view of the same contrast; agreement between it and the model-based test
indicates that the calls are not an artefact of dispersion estimation, although with three
replicates per group it cannot by itself establish significance.

Every number in this report was produced by the workflow in the code repository, run once, in
the container described above. The same workflow run again on the same inputs should reproduce
Supplementary Table S1 byte for byte.

